"Go straight, then turn right."
I remember this instruction from the shopkeeper.
I walk carefully on the street.
First, I go to the right.
Then, I go straight.
"Go towards the sea."
I walk towards the sea.
There are many buildings on this street.
Suddenly, those buildings end.
In front, the sky is wide open.
I reach the wide promenade.
This is Marine Drive.
A cool breeze blows here.
I see the vast sea in front of me.
The water of the sea is very beautiful.
This is the famous road of Mumbai city.
I take a deep breath.
Now I am on the right path.
I am very happy.
